4,"father":"","mother":"Zeruiah","v":[11,15]},{"id":"hadarezer_1340","name":"Hadarezer","also":"Hadadezer","summary":"Hadad is help; called also Hadarezer, Adod is his help, the king of Zobah. Hanun, the king of the Ammonites, hired among others the army of Hadadezer to assist him in his war against David.","verses":18,"father":"Rehob","mother":"","v":[16,19]},{"id":"shobach_2717","name":"Shobach","also":"Shophach","summary":"Poured out, the “captain of the host of Hadarezer” when he mustered his vassals and tributaries from beyond “the river Euphrates” (2 Sam. 10:15-18); called also Shophach (1 Chr. 19:16).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[16,18]}],"places":[{"id":"jericho_634","name":"Jericho","kind":"City","lat":31.87005,"lon":35.44388,"summary":"Place of fragrance, a fenced city in the midst of a vast grove of palm trees, in the plain of Jordan, over against the place where that river was crossed by the Israelites (Josh. 3:16).","verses":58,"v":[5]},{"id":"aram-maacah_83","name":"Aram-maacah","kind":"","lat":33.2,"lon":36.5,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[6]},{"id":"mesopotamia_790","name":"Mesopotamia","kind":"Region","lat":32.5365,"lon":44.42088,"summary":"The country between the two rivers (Heb. Aram-naharaim; i.e., “Syria of the two rivers”), the name given by the Greeks and Romans to the region between the Euphrates and the Tigris (Gen. 24:10; Deut. 23:4; Judg. 3:8, 10).","verses":7,"v":[6]},{"id":"zobah_1272","name":"Zobah","kind":"Region","lat":34.31257,"lon":36.92548,"summary":"Aram-Zobah, (Ps. 60, title), a Syrian province or kingdom to the south of Coele-Syria, and extending from the eastern slopes of Lebanon north and east toward the Euphrates.","verses":11,"v":[6]},{"id":"maacah_743","name":"Maacah","kind":"Region","lat":33.2,"lon":36.5,"summary":"Oppression, a small Syrian kingdom near Geshur, east of the Hauran, the district of Batanea (Josh. 13:13; 2 Sam. 10:6, 8; 1 Chr. 19:7).","verses":4,"v":[7]},{"id":"medeba_775","name":"Medeba","kind":"City","lat":31.72046,"lon":35.79197,"summary":"Waters of quiet, an ancient Moabite town (Num. 21:30). It was assigned to the tribe of Reuben (Josh. 13:16). Here was fought the great battle in which Joab defeated the Ammonites and their allies (1 Chr. 19:7-15; comp. 2 Sam. 10:6-14).","verses":5,"v":[7]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[15]},{"id":"euphrates_421","name":"Euphrates","kind":"Water (River)","lat":34.74942,"lon":40.9364,"summary":"Hebrew, Perath; Assyrian, Purat; Persian cuneiform, Ufratush, whence Greek Euphrates, meaning “sweet water.” The Assyrian name means “the stream,” or “the great stream.”","verses":32,"v":[16]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[17]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[310,310,310,5176,4428,1121,1121,1121,4191,4427,4427,4427,4427,1121,1121],[1732,1732,559,6213,6213,6213,2617,5973,2586,1121,5176,5176,3588,1,1,6213,2617,5973,5973,1732,1732,7971,4397,5162,5162,5162,5921,1,1,1732,1732,1732,5650,935,413,776,776,1121,1121,1121,5162,5162,5162],[8269,8269,1121,1121,1121,559,2586,2586,3588,3588,7971,7971,7971,0,5162,5869,5869,5869,5869,1732,1732,3513,3513,1,1,1,3808,3808,5650,5650,935,413,413,2713,2713,776,776,7270,7270,7270,2015,2015,2015],[2586,2586,3947,1732,5650,1548,1548,1548,3772,3772,4063,4063,5704,4667,4667,7971,7971,7971,7971],[1980,1980,1980,5046,5046,1732,5921,582,582,7971,7971,7122,7122,7122,7122,3588,582,582,1961,1961,3966,3637,4428,4428,559,559,3427,3405,3405,5704,2206,2206,6779,6779,67